{"author":{"id":"6c7374a500bfd4cb191ae45b3f9d4b7a3d9d7f0324d04add217e8cbefeb7e1b9"},"ops":[{"type":3,"timestamp":1793351558,"nonce":"i4M9P0Qpib2wpEeq2ZAxp0EoVek=","message":"Associated issue: 3ec0b2c. Editor allocation milestone committed locally as Ashui 1146207, after 128f37c (66cc2f7) and 0bf8fb0 (0fe11ba / 34d767c).\n\nFresh profiling of actual CodeWorkbench found styling/flush allocation, not evidence of signal contention. Changes: remove the redundant computed between pooled token/gutter data and HXX text; hoist nine CSS enum lookup tables; reuse decoded native CSS responses in a UI-context-local cache, capped at 32 entries / 65,536 serialized characters, excluding entries over 16,384. It contains only decoded strings/maps, no node or native-resource handles. Complete response keys preserve variable/font/context semantics.\n\nThree alternating fresh-process comparisons, 120 switches each, first 20 warm-up, identical native libraries and Ash hybrid/application, 1120x780 at 2x. Median allocated bytes per three-frame switch: source 289.95 -\u003e 230.09 KiB (-20.6%); notes 274.52 -\u003e 216.53 KiB (-21.1%). Median occupied GC blocks after collection: 23.84 -\u003e 23.34 MiB. Startup allocation 27.77 -\u003e 27.51 MiB. Mounted nodes stay 580. The two CodeWorkbench PNGs are byte-identical. Do not infer an interactive latency improvement: timing includes one-pixel GPU completion waits and other verification was running. A preliminary unpaced run is excluded because queued GPU work inflated its footprint.\n\nThe process still uses about 200 MiB in this offscreen harness, so the under-100-MB target and broader loading/GC pressure remain unresolved. This issue stays open. These are measured allocation improvements, not a claim to have fixed the entire memory issue.\n\nValidation: tests/run.sh passes (2715 reported ok lines), all targeted render/editor token/culling/state/atlas/clipping checks pass, StyleSnapshotReuse passes 9 bounds/isolation/lifetime checks, root strict Clippy passes, packaging/publication contracts pass 12 tests. Matching CSS tool was built; demo/snapshot HDLLs were updated and hashes checked. Full method/results/caveats: .ashui/editor-alloc/report.md, comparison.json, logs/*-final-*.log; source/controller adjacent. Regression logs under .ashui/release-audit/logs/. The native commit e2383b6 is still local and must be published before a dependent release. No push.","files":null}]}